ite's castling rights\n- The queen remains centralized and active\n- It maintains pressure while keeping tactical flexibility\n- After the king moves, I can continue developing with threats\n\nThis is a forcing move that gives me the initiative and creates long-term positional advantages by damaging White's king safety.\n\n**Reason:** Q: h4-e4 delivers check while centralizing my queen. It forces White's king to move, permanently losing castling rights, and keeps my queen actively placed in the center where it can coordinate with future piece development. This gives me both immediate tactical pressure and long-term strategic advantages.\n\n**Answer:** Q: h4-e4"}
