o the White king on e1\n2. It attacks the critical f2 square (often a weak point)\n3. It forces White into a defensive position\n4. White will likely have to move the king or block with a piece, disrupting their development\n5. This maintains maximum pressure and initiative\n\n**Answer:** Q: e4-e2"}
